flowchart TB
  MAN[Policy manifest names which layers are authoritative]
  R1[Rank 1 - normative behaviour contract]
  R2[Rank 2 - normative execution mechanics contract]
  R3[Rank 3 - style contract]
  R3C[Conditional long-form prose child]
  R4[Rank 4 - durable preferences]
  R5[Rank 5 - memory pointers]
  TIE[Tie break - rank 1 states a goal, rank 2 forbids the mechanism, rank 2 wins]
  ANNEX[In scope but non normative - generated views, bootstrap policy, liveness, identity, changelog, legacy shim]
  D1[Domain - current fact]
  D2[Domain - durable preference]
  D3[Domain - normative policy]
  D4[Domain - proposal]
  FACTS[Structured registry, status and control layers]
  PROP[Labelled proposal awaiting an operator decision]
  VIEWS[Generated views]
  MAN --> R1
  MAN --> FACTS
  R1 --> R2
  R2 --> R3
  R3 --> R4
  R4 --> R5
  R3 -.-> R3C
  TIE -.-> R2
  ANNEX -. informs, never overrides .-> R1
  D1 -- single owner --> FACTS
  D2 -- single owner --> R4
  D3 -- single owner --> R1
  D4 -- single owner --> PROP
  FACTS -- regenerates --> VIEWS
  VIEWS -. renders from, never overrides .-> FACTS
